        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.97999999999999,
          "end": 114.453,
          "en": "your actual url that leads to your website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.66,
          "end": 117.53,
          "en": "So that is something you want to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.53,
          "end": 121.3,
          "en": "when deploying your application that uses authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.3,
          "end": 123.31,
          "en": "But with that, we're done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.31,
          "end": 127.21,
          "en": "and you now learn how authentication works with Next.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.21,
          "end": 129.98,
          "en": "and how it helps you with authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.98,
          "end": 132.81,
          "en": "And how you can manage users, creating users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.81,
          "end": 135.93,
          "en": "logging users in, protecting pages and routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.93,
          "end": 139.55,
          "en": "changing the UI when users are logging in and logging out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.55,
          "end": 142.853,
          "en": "and how you can also protect your API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.71,
          "end": 147.35,
          "en": "Now it is worth noting that there are more providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.35,
          "end": 150.53,
          "en": "than the Credentials provider we used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.53,
          "end": 153.96,
          "en": "This is the provider where you manage your own users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.96,
          "end": 158.26,
          "en": "with email, password, or whatever your credentials are.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.26,
          "end": 160.72,
          "en": "You can also use a third party provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.72,
          "end": 165.72,
          "en": "like Apple or Amazon or GitHub or Facebook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.78,
          "end": 168.88,
          "en": "All of that is possible as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.88,
          "end": 170.96,
          "en": "You can bring those providers as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.96,
          "end": 172.28,
          "en": "and if you want to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.28,
          "end": 175.34,
          "en": "this kind of authentication to your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.34,
          "end": 177.93,
          "en": "simply check out the NextAuth Docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 177.93,
          "end": 180.09,
          "en": "for that provider you want to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.09,
          "end": 181.32,
          "en": "And you then learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.32,
          "end": 185.83,
          "en": "how you can add that provider to your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.83,
          "end": 190.26,
          "en": "And providers in this NextAuth file which you always need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.26,
          "end": 191.88,
          "en": "providers is an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.88,
          "end": 196.2,
          "en": "so you can always add multiple providers to your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.2,
          "end": 197.37,
          "en": "so that you can offer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.37,
          "end": 201.47,
          "en": "multiple log in alternatives to your users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.47,
          "end": 204.76,
          "en": "So NextAuth is very powerful and flexible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.76,
          "end": 207.593,
          "en": "and in this module, you'll learn how you can use it.",
